@page
@model AboutModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About MatchPredictor";
    ViewData["Description"] = "MatchPredictor is an informational football statistics tool that publishes calibrated daily picks, selection lists, and an honest settled-results track record.";
}

<div class="mp-container mp-legal">
    <div class="mp-page-header">
        <div>
            <p class="mp-page-kicker">About</p>
            <div class="mp-page-title">
                <h1>About MatchPredictor</h1>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mp-legal-meta">
        Contact: <a href="mailto:hello@matchpredictor.dev">hello@matchpredictor.dev</a>
        · <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>
        · <a href="/methodology">How the model works</a>
    </p>

    <section class="mp-legal-section">
        <h2>What this site is</h2>
        <p>
            MatchPredictor is an informational football (soccer) statistics site at
            <strong>matchpredictor.dev</strong>. Each day we publish a curated card of picks across
            Both Teams to Score, Over/Under 2.5 goals, Straight Win, and Draw markets, plus
            auto-composed selection lists and a public settled-results record.
        </p>
        <p>
            We are <strong>not</strong> a bookmaker. We do not accept stakes, hold deposits, or operate
            gambling services. Optional slip-export links open a third-party sportsbook governed by
            its own terms and licensing. The site is intended for users aged <strong>18 and over</strong> only.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mp-legal-section">
        <h2>What we publish</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Daily market cards</strong> — filterable lists of published picks with calibrated confidence, kickoff time, and settlement when the match finishes.</li>
            <li><strong>Selection lists</strong> — curated multi-leg lists (Banker, Rollover, Ladder, and related variants) built from the day’s analysed card.</li>
            <li><strong>Settled results</strong> — an honest recent track record of published picks that have finished, including losses. See <a href="/results">Results</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Methodology</strong> — a plain-language description of how signals are blended, calibrated, and gated before publish. See <a href="/methodology">Methodology</a>.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mp-legal-section">
        <h2>How we think about quality</h2>
        <p>
            A pick only appears on the public card when its calibrated probability clears a
            market-specific publish threshold. After kickoff we settle scores against real results
            and use that history to recalibrate and retune thresholds. Past hit rate is not a
            guarantee of future results — it is a maintenance signal that the site is actively curated.
        </p>
        <p>
            Predictions are statistical estimates. They can be wrong on any given day. Use the tools
            for information and entertainment; never stake more than you can afford to lose.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mp-legal-section">
        <h2>Editorial Team &amp; Research Authorship</h2>
        <p>
            MatchPredictor is maintained by a specialized group of quantitative analysts, data engineers, and football statisticians. Our team designs and validates statistical goal distributions, oversees daily data scraping pipelines, and implements machine learning calibration routines:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Lead Quantitative Modeler:</strong> Oversees bivariate Poisson processes, Dixon-Coles parameter tuning, and Shin margin removal algorithms.</li>
            <li><strong>Sports Analytics &amp; Football Data Specialist:</strong> Curates league fixtures, reviews team news anomalies, and monitors data pipeline integrity across European and domestic competitions.</li>
            <li><strong>Machine Learning &amp; Calibration Engineer:</strong> Manages nightly Brier score evaluations, out-of-sample holdout validation, and isotonic regression calibration models.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Explore our educational publications and research papers in our <a href="/guides">Football Analytics Guides</a> hub.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mp-legal-section">
        <h2>Who runs it</h2>
        <p>
            MatchPredictor is operated as an independent analytical project focused on football probability
            modelling and transparent daily publication. There are no user accounts and we do not
            sell personal data. For privacy details see our <a href="/Privacy">Privacy Policy</a>;
            for usage rules see our <a href="/terms">Terms of Use</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
            Questions, corrections, or inquiries: <a href="mailto:hello@matchpredictor.dev">hello@matchpredictor.dev</a> · <a href="/contact">Contact Page</a>.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mp-legal-section">
        <h2>Responsible use</h2>
        <p>
            MatchPredictor is an informational statistics tool intended for users aged 18 and older. We are not a bookmaker and do not take bets. If sports entertainment is affecting you or someone you know, seek confidential, free help from a recognised support organisation:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="https://www.begambleaware.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">BeGambleAware.org</a> (UK National Gambling Helpline: 0808 8020 133)</li>
            <li><a href="https://www.gamcare.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">GamCare.org.uk</a></li>
            <li><a href="/Privacy#responsible-use">MatchPredictor Responsible Use Policy</a></li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
